{"content":[{"c":["DUMAH (P",{"c":["lace"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Region of the 12 tribes of Ishmael (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.25.14","r":"Gen.25.14","rawR":"Gen.25.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.25.14","value":"Gen.25.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 25:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.30","r":"1Chr.1.30","rawR":"1Chr.1.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.30","value":"1Chr.1.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:30"},") where there were a number of oases; identified with el-Jof, modern Dumat el-Jendel. This place was located about three-fourths of the way from Damascus to Medina."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Town in the highlands allotted to Judah’s tribe for an inheritance (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.52","r":"Josh.15.52","rawR":"Josh.15.52","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.52","value":"Josh.15.52"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:52"},"). Its site is probably identifiable with ed-Domeh, 10 miles (16.1 kilometers) southwest of Hebron."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Hebrew term referring to the land of silence or death; that is, the place of graves (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.94.17","r":"Ps.94.17","rawR":"Ps.94.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.94.17","value":"Ps.94.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 94:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.115.17","r":"Ps.115.17","rawR":"Ps.115.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.115.17","value":"Ps.115.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"115:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Perhaps a designation for Edom or Idumea in ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.21.11","r":"Isa.21.11","rawR":"Isa.21.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.21.11","value":"Isa.21.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isaiah 21:11"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"DumahPlace","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 25:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.25.14","rawQueryValue":"Gen.25.14","